why: operator instruction 2026-09-08 — file every problem case from
  the bench-refresh results into BACKLOG.md, then start fixing. The
  entries go in FIRST and as their own lane, so they survive whether
  or not the fixing that follows stalls; AGENTS.md wants found-but-
  deferred work in the backlog the moment it is found.

what: one entry per finding, each carrying what the `performance`
  skill requires before anyone starts: the ratio and its TWIN, the
  expected size of the win, and the DISQUALIFYING evidence — what
  result would say the theory is wrong. An entry that cannot name its
  disqualifying evidence is not ready and says so.

  Grouped, because three of them are one defect: `default-not-measured`
  (fork/join, many-to-many, cancel — in each the library already
  contains a faster answer and the DEFAULT does not choose it).

predict: no code in this lane. The gate runs because the rule says so.
